    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** A pivot toward AI and high-performance computing is evident with a large-scale colocation profit-sharing deal, signaling demand for compute capacity. However, sentiment is heavily contested: short interest surged dramatically, and Nasdaq issued a delisting determination over equity shortfalls, though management asserts compliance has since been restored. Legal victories have reduced liabilities, but extreme market skepticism persists.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is rebranding to Big Digital Energy, contesting the Nasdaq delisting via a hearing, and formed a strategic transactions committee to evaluate M&A and joint ventures. Board reconstitution and independent committee approval of the related-party colocation deal signal governance improvements. Yet a Weiss Ratings sell call and the spike in short interest indicate the market has not yet bought into the turnaround narrative.",
